,"summary":"The National Museum and Art Gallery is the national museum of Trinidad and Tobago, in Port of Spain on Trinidad island. It is located at the top of Frederick Street, opposite the Memorial Park, and just south of the Queen's Park Savannah.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"National Museum and Art Gallery, Trinidad","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Trinidad_national_museum_2006-23-02.JPG/1280px-Trinidad_national_museum_2006-23-02.JPG","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Trinidad_national_museum_2006-23-02.JPG/500px-Trinidad_national_museum_2006-23-02.JPG","w":1200,"h":800,"author":"Wikimedia Commons contributor","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trinidad_national_museum_2006-23-02.JPG"}},{"id":"trinidad_and_tobago_el_tucuche","areaId":"trinidad_and_tobago","name":"El Tucuche","category":"viewpoint","tags":["mountains","views","hiking"],"location":{"lat":10.73333,"lng":-61.41667},"visitMinutes":180,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"trinidad_and_tobago_el_tucuche","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":0,"wikiPageviews":199,"wikidataSitelinks":11,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13"},"hashtags":["eltucuche","trinidadandtobago"],"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"El Tucuche is the second highest peak in Trinidad's Northern Range and is noted for its interesting pyramidal shape. It is fabled in Amerindian lore as a sacred mountain. There are Amerindian petroglyphs on a rock outcrop below the mountain. These are the only petroglyphs in the country known to archaeologists.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"El Tucuche","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/El_Tucuche_45.jpg/1280px-El_Tucuche_45.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/El_Tucuche_45.jpg/500px-El_Tucuche_45.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"bnd