 of Spain, Trinidad and Tobago. It is the seat of the Archdiocese of Port of Spain. Construction started in 1816 and it was completed in 1851. The same year the cathedral was given the honorary status of a minor basilica.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Cathedral of the Immaculate Conception (Port of Spain)","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Cathedral_Basilica_of_the_Immaculate_Conception_%28Port_of_Spain%29.JPG/1280px-Cathedral_Basilica_of_the_Immaculate_Conception_%28Port_of_Spain%29.JPG","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Cathedral_Basilica_of_the_Immaculate_Conception_%28Port_of_Spain%29.JPG/500px-Cathedral_Basilica_of_the_Immaculate_Conception_%28Port_of_Spain%29.JPG","w":1200,"h":1800,"author":"1Parishioner","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cathedral_Basilica_of_the_Immaculate_Conception_(Port_of_Spain).JPG"}},{"id":"trinidad_and_tobago_hasely_crawford_stadium","areaId":"trinidad_and_tobago","name":"Hasely Crawford Stadium","category":"other","tags":["family"],"location":{"lat":10.66152,"lng":-61.53303},"visitMinutes":90,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"trinidad_and_tobago_hasely_crawford_stadium","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":1,"commonsNearby":0,"wikiPageviews":837,"wikidataSitelinks":21,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13"},"hashtags":["haselycrawfordstadium","trinidadandtobago"],"summary":"The Hasely Crawford Stadium, formerly the National Stadium, is located in Port of Spain, Trinidad and Tobago. It was inaugurated and formally opened by Prime Minister George Chambers on 12 June 1982.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Hasely Crawford Stadium","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b2/HCStadium2013.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b2/HCStadium2013.jpg","w":1200,"h":614,"author":"Chris Fitzpatrick","license":"CC 